Subject: Re: Upgrade from RPostgresql 0.3-3 to 0.4 (just this week) breaks our query - TIMESTAMP not coming through correctly?
In-Reply-To: <53A252DA.5060000@pacificedge.co.nz>
References: <53A23222.7030209@pacificedge.co.nz> <9B0BA4BE-960E-4858-B8B3-E6A0BCA291E2@staff.kanazawa-u.ac.jp> <53A252DA.5060000@pacificedge.co.nz>
Message-ID: <A4B3CFD6-E20C-42E2-81E2-0D7BBBC3BDE3@staff.kanazawa-u.ac.jp>

Dear Mark,

If you need world-wide support, 
SET timezone to 'UTC'
as http://www.postgresql.org/docs/9.3/static/sql-set.html
at the begining or
AT TIME ZONE zone 'UTC'
(as explained in http://www.postgresql.org/docs/9.2/static/functions-datetime.html#FUNCTIONS-DATETIME-ZONECONVERT)
for each query might help as a workaround option.

The data transfer is done as a character string anyway, and the problem is whether the
string can be interpreted as a proper time data.

-- 
Tomoaki NISHIYAMA

